    "created_at": "2016-02-08T10:44:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-08T10:44:18Z",
    "body": "It looks like the first sign of this is in d929dff377ff346bb584e8f3c3ec5992aa7990d5, \"Prevent nesting `<time>`, `<meter>`, `<progress>`.\" Then `<time>` was replaced by `<data>` in 70b0ce45a26937a3f26eeb72b146261ff6210a1d, and when it was revived in 92baa8333203ea5b97316bb1775331b216d55dab, the current phrasing was used.\n\nNote that both `<meter>` and `<progress>` keep the limited restriction in the original form, saying \"Phrasing content, but there must be no meter/progress element descendants.\"\n\nCurrently, `<date datetime=2016-02-08><date>2016-02-08</date></date>` is valid but `<date><date datetime=2016-02-08>2016-02-08</date></date>` is not, which seems weird, both are silly.\n\nSo how about going back to \"no time element descendants\" plus the \"must match requirements described in prose below\" recently added?\n",
