    "body": "I have no strong opinion here.\n\nNote that there's a huge difference between child text nodes and descendant text nodes in any dynamic environment. Child nodes involve a single pointer test. Descendant dependencies require comparatively huge infrastructure. Any text node modifications have to do a tree walk up to the root just in case there's a time element descendant (or you have to maintain a bit throughout the tree regarding whether you have such an ancestor).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
