    "created_at": "2016-02-23T18:57:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-23T18:57:24Z",
    "body": "> I think that concept is used by `style`, `script`, `title`.\n\nRight—and IMHO that’s the model we should (re)use for `time`, but doing that the right way means the behavior of HTML parsers would need to be changed to handle `time` that way (and of course the HTML parsing algorithm would need to be changed to require parsers/browsers to process `time` that way).\n\nPractically speaking, I’m not sure if implementors are going to be enthusiastic at this point about changing their HTML parsers just for this. So if it seems like we’re not likely to get parsers/browsers to implement a change here, then I think we should drop the _\"A `time` element that does not have a `datetime` content attribute must not have any element descendants\"_ authoring requirement.\n",
