    "created_at": "2016-02-25T08:31:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-25T08:31:22Z",
    "body": "> The concept of only looking at **child** Text nodes, and ignoring elements (if you put them there using DOM API or XHTML syntax), is used by `style`, `script`, `title`.\n> …\n> text IDL attribute\n\nThanks—so for the record here, [the language for the relevant requirement in the spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#dom-title-text) is:\n\n> The IDL attribute `text` must return a concatenation of the contents of all the `Text` nodes that are children of the `title`|`script`|`style` element (ignoring any other nodes such as comments or elements), in tree order.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
